{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfBTp43K3ZdLwgNKbLSEq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted index 2 (Fe 0.84 / Sb 0.16), which had the highest EQE I measured at 0.467%. I used all 3 merit measurements. The two most Fe-rich compositions (indices 0 and 1) were never measured, and they may be better still.\n\n**What XRD showed:** I spent 4 of the 5 XRD scans, at indices 3, 9, 14 and 22. From 18% to 48% Sb (indices 3, 9, 14) there was one rutile-type phase, the crystal structure of FeSbO4. At 73% Sb (index 22) extra peaks appeared, probably from a second Sb oxide phase. XRD didn't separate compositions in the Fe-rich half, so I chose the EQE samples by composition.\n\n**EQE results:**\n\n| Index | Fe fraction | EQE (%) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 14 | 0.52 | 0.0034 |\n| 7 | 0.72 | 0.071 |\n| 2 | 0.84 | 0.467 |\n\nEQE rose about 140-fold from the near 1:1 composition to index 2, and it was still rising at the last point I measured. The best composition could be closer to the Fe-rich end than index 2. I included that in the submission as an untested possibility."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":597,"cache_read_input_tokens":9403,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":597},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1631d07b-c306-447b-8b80-74c47168c2f7","uuid":"541286be-6c9c-4e51-915e-c1accfe05708","timestamp":"2026-09-18T19:33:02.466Z","request_id":"req_011CfBTp3bX7MpCwN6c4UzMM"}
